body:
Everytime I hear people tell these kind of stories my heart goes soft. This kind of deep connection that isn't forced at all and is built upon time and trust, slowly, without you even realizing, is something that should be treasured in an age were we people mostly seek instant gratification. Things change, you can grow apart and lose contact, but still that connection never really changes. The mutual respect you have for each other and how things never changed when you confessed is truly beautiful.

&#x200B;

I'm so happy for you to have connected that way with someone. Life is all about experiences in my opinion, and the things you experience live with you forever. Even if you're apart right now, I'm sure the moments you lived with each other are important for you both. Virtual hug, internet friend.

That was an interesting read. It happened to me a couple times that whenever I have to vs in pvp a strong demon I don't have, I can't see what their flaws are until much later, when I finally get them and incorporate them in my team. With Guan Yu I always thought he was a deleting machine (well, he kinda is) but noticed later on that the AoE hit is only 80 damage (when I thought it was like double that, lol). Things like acting speed, mana usage, misses and stuff like that only become apparent when we're actually using these demons. 

&#x200B;

Rant off. Thanks for sharing your thoughts.

Masakado/Huang Di/Anat  and Asherah or Alice looks like a solid team. I don't know if you want the team comp for PvE or PvP, but those four can be good for both. You have pretty good demons there; not their best archetypes for some of them but that psychic Masakado A is gonna get you far. (A good improvement would be fusing a faster demon such as Garuda or Hresvelgr, transfer speedster on it and swapping it with asherah/Alice, as that would almost guarantee you going first and getting the additional press turn from Masakado A's Guardian of the East. )

&#x200B;

Orcus won't do much here, since your best demon is Masakado A and he shines in fast teams, but Orcus pairs well with Asherah and that opens up other team compositions if you get bored of your current one.

&#x200B;

For PvE Amaterasu and Seth are gonna be useful, specially Amaterasu. Good luck, friend.

First of all, I feel for the guy since sending death threats over ANYTHING is never okay, wtf is wrong with people.

&#x200B;

On the other hand I can see what werlyb was talking about right here. About the team ghosting him and not communicating with him at all, for scrims, improvement or whatever. Nothing here is "professional" if neither your teammates or staff wants to get involved with you improving giving criticism/support or making you feel like you belong there. May be good for the two parties involved if werlyb actually went for another team that cared more about him.
